            "review_title": "Review at Noriboi - Omakase Japanese Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Tan P\n1 contribution\n0\nHighly recommended!\nJul 2025 • Family\nMy family and I stumbled upon Noriboi Omakase, a hidden gem that we didn’t expect to steal our hearts. Tucked away in a vibrant center of Ho Chi Minh City near Ben Thanh. This restaurant delivered an unforgettable dining experience that blended Vietnamese fusion with the authenticity and freshness of Japanese cuisine.\n\nDuring our visit in Ho Chi Minh City, we wanted to experience Omakase in Vietnam. We came across Noriboi, a warm ambiance and attentive staff made us feel VIP :). The menu was a delightful surprise, weaving together bold Vietnamese fusion with the delicate precision of Japanese techniques. Each dish was a testament to the passion and skill of Chef Cong, a young and remarkably talented chef whose attention to detail shone through in every bite. His innovative approach—marrying the zesty, aromatic profiles of Vietnam with the clean, umami-rich essence of Japan—was nothing short of extraordinary.\n\nOur family savored every course, from the vibrant herb-infused and Betel leaves the perfectly seared sushi that tasted as if it had been plucked straight from the sea. The freshness of the ingredients was undeniable, and the presentation was as meticulous as it was beautiful. Chef Cong took a moment to chat with us, sharing his inspiration and enthusiasm for his craft, which made the experience all the more special.\n\nNoriboi Omake is a must-visit for anyone craving a unique culinary adventure. We left with full hearts and happy palates, already planning our next trip back to Vietnam just to dine here again. Highly recommended!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten July 31, 2025",
            "rating": 5.0,
